<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-AWB Australian wheat indicator prices - Feb 10.</title>
<headline>RTRS-AWB Australian wheat indicator prices - Feb 10.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian Wheat Board international card prices for wheat exports for Feb 10.</p>
<p>In U.S. dollars per tonne, FOB eastern states.</p>
<p>		ASW	  AH     PH 13 PCT  PH 14 PCT</p>
<p>    Feb    199.00    203.50    206.00     218.00</p>
<p>    Mar    199.00    203.50    206.00     218.00</p>
<p>    Apr    198.00    202.50    205.00     218.00</p>
<p>    May    198.00    202.50    205.00     218.00</p>
<p>    Jun    198.00    202.50    205.00     218.00</p>
<p>    Jul    196.50    201.00    203.50     216.50</p>
<p>Note: ASW = Australian Standard White; AH = Australian Hard; PH = Australian Prime Hard; percentages = protein content.</p>
<p>Australian Wheat Board indicator prices for multi-grade contracts for 1997/98 crop wheat decreased by A$2.00 a tonne.</p>
<p>	  Indicator Prices in A$ per tonne:</p>
<p>		  ASW 10 pct protein</p>
<p>National FOB	165.00</p>
<p>Indicator prices on a delivered port basis:</p>
<p>Queensland			   South Australia</p>
<p>    Mackay	  140.50	    Port Adelaide	 142.00</p>
<p>    Gladstone     140.75	    Port Giles	    142.75</p>
<p>    Brisbane	138.50	    Wallaroo		140.50</p>
<p>    New South Wales		   Pt Pirie		137.50</p>
<p>    Newcastle     140.50	    Pt Lincoln	    143.75</p>
<p>    Port Kembla   141.00	    Thevenard	     138.75</p>
<p>    Victoria			     Western Australia</p>
<p>    Geelong	 140.00	     Esperance	    145.25</p>
<p>    Portland	141.00	     Albany		 146.25</p>
<p>					     Fremantle	    148.25</p>
<p>					     Geraldton	    146.25</p>
<p>NOTE: The indicator price represents the current state of the international wheat market. It is a cash contract price quoted on a delivered port basis, offered today by the AWB for wheat delivered during the 1997/98 harvest. The offer is valid</p>
<p>until 4.30 p.m. Australian Eastern Standard Summer Time (0530 GMT).</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
